  "description": "A high-performance object-to-object mapper for .NET. Mapping delegates are\n      compiled once per type pair via Expression Trees and cached for the lifetime\n      of the IMapper instance — no reflection, no boxing, on the hot path.\n      Supports bi-directional mapping, property flattening, unflattening, nullable\n      coercion, numeric widening, enum conversion, collection mapping with DFS\n      cycle detection, and EF Core-compatible ProjectTo SQL projection.\n      v3.0 added mapping into an existing instance, ConstructUsing for types without\n      a parameterless constructor, per-member Condition and NullSubstitute, BeforeMap\n      / AfterMap lifecycle hooks, configurable recursion depth (MaxDepth) for\n      self-referencing types, and AssertConfigurationIsValid startup validation.\n      v4.0 added collection merge into an existing collection, configurable\n      flatten/unflatten lookahead depth (FlattenDepth), reusable IValueResolver\n      classes for ForMember, polymorphic/inheritance mapping (Include), and\n      recursive AssertConfigurationIsValid into nested complex-type pairs.\n      v5.0 adds DI-resolved value resolvers (MapFrom<TResolver,TMember>()\n      via a Mapper constructed with an IServiceProvider), ForAllMembers blanket\n      per-pair member rules, and identity-based collection diffing\n      (EqualityComparison) for add/update/remove merges into an existing collection.\n      v5.1 extends Include-based polymorphic dispatch beyond top-level calls: elements\n      of a mapped collection and nested complex members now map on their runtime type\n      (a Dog inside a List<Animal>, or a nested Animal member holding a Dog, maps\n      to DogDto), paid only for pairs that declare Include<>.",
